/// has been deleted, and re-encrypts the token vault with an Amazon Web
/// Services managed key so that you can use the token vault again. This
/// operation can't be undone. The reset permanently deletes the OAuth2
/// access tokens and refresh tokens stored in the token vault, including
/// tokens obtained through all supported flows. After the reset, your
/// agents must complete these flows again to get new tokens, and for
/// user-delegated flows your users must authorize access again. The reset
/// doesn't delete your credential providers or their configuration. You can
/// reset a token vault only if its customer managed key has been deleted.
/// If the key still exists, including when it's disabled or scheduled for
